acadrust is used unmodified, as a separate library, linked from crates.io. AfroBIM's own code
is not covered by the MPL. The Source Code Form of acadrust, the Covered Software, is available
at the addresses above; anyone who receives AfroBIM in Executable Form may obtain it there
under the terms of the MPL-2.0. If AfroBIM ever ships a modified copy of any acadrust file,
that file stays under the MPL-2.0 and its source must be made available with the change.

acadrust's own third-party notice (THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md) states that its DWG reader and
writer include code ported and adapted from ACadSharp, below.

