==============================================================================
Map tile and imagery providers
==============================================================================

AfroBIM can fetch map tiles and satellite imagery over the internet when the user asks it to
(MAPCAPTURE and the basemap). The tiles are not part of AfroBIM and are not bundled. They belong
to their providers, whose terms the user must follow, including any limit on commercial use,
bulk download or storage. The attribution each provider asks for is shown in the app and is
written on every capture. The providers, with their attribution text, are listed in
afrobim/crates/afrobim-raster/src/tiles.rs and are:

  Esri (World Imagery, Street, Topographic, Shaded Relief, Gray Canvas): Imagery (c) Esri, Maxar,
      Earthstar Geographics and the GIS User Community. https://www.esri.com/en-us/legal/terms
  OpenStreetMap, OpenStreetMap Humanitarian (HOT), OpenTopoMap: (c) OpenStreetMap contributors,
      Open Database Licence 1.0. https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright
      OpenTopoMap style (c) OpenTopoMap (CC BY-SA); SRTM data.
  CARTO (Voyager, Positron, Dark Matter): (c) CARTO, with OpenStreetMap contributors.
  EOX Sentinel-2 cloudless: EOX IT Services GmbH, containing modified Copernicus Sentinel data.
      The 2020 layer is CC BY-NC-SA 4.0 (non-commercial); the 2016 layer has its own terms.
  Mapbox, MapTiler, Thunderforest, Stadia Maps, Microsoft Azure Maps: only with the user's own
      access key, under the user's own account terms. (c) of each provider and of OpenStreetMap
      contributors and the imagery suppliers named in the app.

Using the free tile services inside a commercial product may need a paid plan or written
permission. The user, not AfroBIM, accepts those terms when choosing a provider.

==============================================================================
Rule packs and transport fonts
==============================================================================

The rule packs in packs/ hold values transcribed from published road traffic sign manuals (UK
Department for Transport Traffic Signs Manual and TSRGD 2016; Uganda Ministry of Works and
Transport Traffic Signs Manual, 2004). Contains public sector information licensed under the
Open Government Licence v3.0 where that licence applies
(https://www.nationalarchives.gov.uk/doc/open-government-licence/version/3/). The status of
each pack is being confirmed with the rights holders. The Uganda pack is published by AfroBIM for
use on Ministry of Works and Transport projects.

The Transport fonts (Key Transport Medium and Key Transport Heavy, version 1.003) are Copyright
Keysoft Solutions, based on fonts supplied by cbrd.co.uk. They are included for drawing traffic
signs and remain the property of their owner; they are not covered by the AfroBIM EULA.
